WEBVTT

00:00.500 --> 00:04.890
Which of the following
numbers is a factor of 154?

00:04.890 --> 00:07.240
So when a number is going
to be a factor of 154

00:07.240 --> 00:10.020
is if we can divide
that number into 154

00:10.020 --> 00:11.554
and not have a remainder.

00:11.554 --> 00:13.470
Or another way of thinking
about it-- a number

00:13.470 --> 00:19.250
is a factor of 154 if 154 is
a multiple of that number.

00:19.250 --> 00:22.060
So let's look at each of these
and see which of these we

00:22.060 --> 00:24.420
can rule out or say is a factor.

00:24.420 --> 00:27.309
So does 3 divide
evenly into 154?

00:27.309 --> 00:28.850
Or, another way of
thinking about it,

00:28.850 --> 00:32.172
is 154 a multiple of 3?

00:32.172 --> 00:34.130
Well you'll later learn
that you could actually

00:34.130 --> 00:36.640
test whether something
is divisible by 3

00:36.640 --> 00:37.890
by adding up the digits.

00:37.890 --> 00:39.870
And if that's divisible
by 3, then it's

00:39.870 --> 00:41.760
going to be divisible by 3.

00:41.760 --> 00:43.690
And so you see
here, 1 plus 5 is 6.

00:43.690 --> 00:46.280
6 plus 4 is 10.

00:46.280 --> 00:48.431
10 is not divisible by 3.

00:48.431 --> 00:50.430
But if you didn't want
to do that little trick--

00:50.430 --> 00:51.480
and we have other
videos where we

00:51.480 --> 00:53.350
go into more detail
about that trick--

00:53.350 --> 00:58.170
you can actually just
divide 3 into 154.

00:58.170 --> 00:59.260
3 doesn't go into 1.

00:59.260 --> 01:02.060
It does go into 15 five times.

01:02.060 --> 01:04.170
5 times 3 is 15.

01:04.170 --> 01:05.190
Subtract.

01:05.190 --> 01:06.710
Then we have 0.

01:06.710 --> 01:08.910
Then you bring down a 4.

01:08.910 --> 01:10.960
3 goes into 4 one time.

01:10.960 --> 01:12.520
1 times 3 is 3.

01:12.520 --> 01:15.690
Subtract, and you
have a remainder of 1.

01:15.690 --> 01:21.160
So 3 is clearly not a factor of
154, so we can rule that out.

01:21.160 --> 01:22.830
Now what about 5?

01:22.830 --> 01:24.900
Well, any multiple
of 5 is either

01:24.900 --> 01:27.900
going to have 5 or
0 in the ones place.

01:27.900 --> 01:31.290
You see that if we write 5
times 1 is 5, 5 times 2 is 10,

01:31.290 --> 01:37.150
5 times 3 is 15, 5 times 4 is
20, you either have a 5 or a 0

01:37.150 --> 01:38.400
in the ones place.

01:38.400 --> 01:40.960
This does not have 5
or a 0 the ones place,

01:40.960 --> 01:43.610
so it's not going to
be divisible by 5.

01:43.610 --> 01:45.130
5 is not a factor.

01:45.130 --> 01:49.070
154 is not a multiple of 5.

01:49.070 --> 01:50.044
Now 6 is interesting.

01:50.044 --> 01:51.210
You could do the same thing.

01:51.210 --> 01:53.890
You could try to
divide 6 into 154.

01:53.890 --> 01:55.927
But if something
is divisible by 6,

01:55.927 --> 01:58.010
it's definitely going to
be divisible by 3 as well

01:58.010 --> 01:59.950
because 6 is divisible by 3.

01:59.950 --> 02:02.080
So we can immediately
rule this one out as well.

02:02.080 --> 02:05.480
Because 154 is not
divisible by 3,

02:05.480 --> 02:07.590
it's also not going
to be divisible by 6.

02:07.590 --> 02:09.419
And you could try
it out if you like.

02:09.419 --> 02:11.540
And we could make the
same argument for 9.

02:11.540 --> 02:14.990
If something is divisible by 9,
it's going to be divisible by 3

02:14.990 --> 02:16.540
because 9 is divisible by 3.

02:16.540 --> 02:18.810
Well, it's not
divisible by 3, so we're

02:18.810 --> 02:20.241
going to rule out 9 as well.

02:20.241 --> 02:21.490
So we've ruled out everything.

02:21.490 --> 02:23.360
It looks like 14
is our only option,

02:23.360 --> 02:24.960
but let's actually verify it.

02:24.960 --> 02:29.940
Let's actually
divide 14 into 154.

02:29.940 --> 02:31.570
14 doesn't go into 1.

02:31.570 --> 02:34.360
It goes into 15
exactly one time.

02:34.360 --> 02:36.570
1 times 14 is 14.

02:36.570 --> 02:37.840
We subtract.

02:37.840 --> 02:39.060
We get 1.

02:39.060 --> 02:40.230
Bring down the 4.

02:40.230 --> 02:43.150
14 goes into 14 one time.

02:43.150 --> 02:44.660
1 times 14 is 14.

02:44.660 --> 02:46.790
And of course, we
have no remainder.

02:46.790 --> 02:50.750
So 14 goes into 154
exactly 11 times.

02:50.750 --> 02:53.280
Or 11 times 14 is 154.

02:53.280 --> 02:56.940
154 is a multiple of 14.

02:56.940 --> 02:58.490
Let's do one more.

02:58.490 --> 03:01.122
Which of the following
numbers is a multiple of 14?

03:01.122 --> 03:02.580
So now we have 14,
and we're trying

03:02.580 --> 03:04.610
to think of its multiples.

03:04.610 --> 03:06.600
So there's two
ways of doing this.

03:06.600 --> 03:09.824
You could go number by number
and try to divide 14 into them,

03:09.824 --> 03:11.240
or we could just
try to figure out

03:11.240 --> 03:13.620
what all of the multiples
of 14 actually are.

03:13.620 --> 03:14.620
So let's try to do that.

03:14.620 --> 03:16.390
Let's try to do that
second technique.

03:16.390 --> 03:20.810
14 times 1 is 14.

03:20.810 --> 03:21.795
You add another 14.

03:21.795 --> 03:24.010
14 times 2 is 28.

03:24.010 --> 03:25.274
Add another 14.

03:25.274 --> 03:26.190
Let's see, you add 10.

03:26.190 --> 03:27.150
You get to 38.

03:27.150 --> 03:28.600
Then you add 4 more.

03:28.600 --> 03:31.210
You get to 42.

03:31.210 --> 03:32.430
Then you add another 14.

03:32.430 --> 03:34.580
I haven't seen any of
these numbers show up yet.

03:34.580 --> 03:36.840
Add another 14 to this.

03:36.840 --> 03:40.440
You get to 56-- still
not quite there.

03:40.440 --> 03:42.006
Add another 14.

03:42.006 --> 03:43.630
Let's see, if you
add 4, you get to 60,

03:43.630 --> 03:44.754
and you have to add the 10.

03:44.754 --> 03:46.870
So then you get to 70.

03:46.870 --> 03:49.560
And it looks like we have
found one of these numbers.

03:49.560 --> 03:52.070
70 is a multiple of 14.

03:52.070 --> 03:59.268
14 times 1, 2, 3, 4,
5-- 14 times 5 is 70.
